+## Adopting lean execution
+
+Lean execution lets the coordinator run the mechanical stages itself (Tasks-to-Issues, Execute
+coordination, Ready and PR, and fixed QA collection commands) instead of launching a delegated
+agent for them. It is already on for features fixed at the `lite` and `standard` tiers unless the
+policy sets `enabled: false`; other features need the opt-in in `.specify/workflow.yml`:
+
+```yaml
+lean_execution:
+  enabled: true
+```
+
+Never change this setting while a claim is active: finish or release the claim first. Each feature's
+checkpoint keeps the policy it was bound to, and a change to `lean_execution` counts as reaching
+Execute, so the best moment is between features or before a feature reaches Execute. A feature that
+already holds an Execute receipt reports `policy-changed` and re-runs Execute and the stages after it.
+The setting moves coordination work only. Independent review, the selected QA and User Manual semantics, model
+allowlists, separate E2E authoring and collection, claim binding and candidate acceptance stay
+exactly as they are, and every stage still records its receipt.
+
